title: A Law unto Itself
subtitle: A district leader ignores the Zentrale.
new-page: true
tags: event
priority: -1
view-if: {!
if (typeof RG === 'undefined') { return false; }
if (!RG.lw && this.game.scenes.lw_lib) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.lw_lib.onArrival); }
return !!(RG.lw && RG.lw.ready('rogue_leader'));
!}
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.lw) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.lw_lib.onArrival); }
RG.lw.fire('rogue_leader');
Q.lw_name = Q.lw_dc_has ? Q.lw_dc_name : 'the district secretary';
!}

= A Law unto Itself

In **[+ lw_d_name +]**, [? if lw_dc_has = 1 : **[+ lw_dc_name +]** ?][? if lw_dc_has = 0 : the district secretary ?] has stopped pretending. The district follows the [+ lw_d_fname +], and its leadership now prints its own leaflets, calls its own meetings and answers the Zentrale's circulars with a postcard, when it answers at all.

Last week, at a meeting in [+ lw_town +], [? if lw_dc_has = 1 : [+ lw_dc_name +] ?][? if lw_dc_has = 0 : the secretary ?] said that the Zentrale in Berlin "knows the working class from the newspapers". The hall cheered.

- @summon: Summon [+ lw_name +] to Berlin.
- @coopt: Bring [+ lw_name +] into the Zentrale.
- @remove: Remove the district leadership.
- @tolerate: Let it go.

@summon
subtitle: A test of the Zentrale's authority. It may end in a handshake, or in an open break.
on-arrival: {!
var p = 0.3 + RG.num(Q['district_' + Q.lw_d + '_loyalty']) / 100 + RG.num(Q.unity) / 200;
if (Math.random() < p) {
    Q.lw_out = 1;
    RG.district(Q.lw_d, {loyalty: 10});
    Q.unity += 2;
} else {
    Q.lw_out = 2;
    RG.district(Q.lw_d, {loyalty: -5});
    Q.unity -= 3;
    RG.lw.lean(Q.lw_d_faction, 1, 3);
    RG.news('District leadership in ' + Q.lw_d_name + ' defies the Zentrale');
}
!}

[? if lw_out = 1 : The meeting in the Zentrale lasts until two in the morning and ends with a handshake and a joint statement. The district will follow the line, and the line will mention the district. ?][? if lw_out = 2 : The telegram comes back: too busy with the class struggle to travel. The district committee prints the exchange in its own bulletin. ?]

@coopt
subtitle: The district comes back into the fold. The Zentrale's own current resents the newcomer.
on-arrival: {!
RG.district(Q.lw_d, {loyalty: 12});
RG.lw.lean(Q.lw_d_faction, 1, 6);
Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] -= 5;
Q.unity += 1;
if (Q.lw_dc_has) {
    RG.setRole(Q.lw_dc, 'Member of the Zentrale');
    RG.news(Q.lw_dc_name + ' joins the Zentrale');
} else {
    RG.news('The secretary of ' + Q.lw_d_name + ' joins the Zentrale');
}
!}

A seat at the long table in Berlin changes a man's view of the Zentrale, at least for a while. The district's bulletin prints the Zentrale's resolutions again, on the front page.

@remove
subtitle: The Zentrale shows who leads. The district may come over, or bleed members.
on-arrival: {!
Q.unity -= 3;
RG.lw.lean(Q.lw_d_faction, 0, -8);
Q[Q.leading_faction + '_satisfaction'] += 3;
if (Q.lw_dc_has) { RG.setRole(Q.lw_dc, 'Removed from the district leadership'); }
if (Math.random() < 0.5) {
    Q.lw_out = 1;
    Q['district_' + Q.lw_d + '_faction'] = Q.leading_faction;
    Q['district_' + Q.lw_d + '_loyalty'] = 45;
    RG.district(Q.lw_d, {members: -0.06});
} else {
    Q.lw_out = 2;
    RG.district(Q.lw_d, {members: -0.12, loyalty: -8});
}
RG.news('Zentrale dissolves the district committee in ' + Q.lw_d_name);
!}

The Zentrale's instructors arrive with a letter of dismissal and a new set of keys for the office. [? if lw_out = 1 : After a stormy district conference, a committee loyal to Berlin is elected. Some old members tear up their cards in the hall. ?][? if lw_out = 2 : Half the district walks out with its old leaders. Those who stay are loyal, and few. ?]

@tolerate
subtitle: No fight now. The district drifts further from the Zentrale, and its current grows bolder.
on-arrival: {!
RG.district(Q.lw_d, {loyalty: -4});
RG.lw.lean(Q.lw_d_faction, 1, 4);
Q.unity -= 2;
!}

The Zentrale decides that a quarrel with [+ lw_d_name +] is the last thing the party needs. [+ lw_d_name +] draws its own conclusions.
